  "question": {
    "text": "A graph is plotted between log (x/m) and log P according to the equation <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></math> .<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0035_dd5e0840a756.jpg\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 123px;\" /><br />\r<br />\rWhich of the following statements about this graph is not correct?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "The figure shows Freundlich adsorption isotherm",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "The figure shows Langmuir adsorption isotherm",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "The adsorption varies with pressure",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "The factor 1/n can have values between 0 and 1",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "This is Freundlich isotherm not Langmuir.<br /><br />It is also written as<br /><br /><math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow></mrow></math><br /><br />where<br /><br />x = mass of adsorbate<br /><br />m = mass of adsorbent<br /><br />p = Equilibrium pressure of adsorbate<br /><br />K and n are constants for a given adsorbate and adsorbent at a particular temperature."
  }
